      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d rather we don\u0027t call a method that reads members in a helper method that\u0027s called by the constructor. Consider :\n\n  class Foo {\n    @NonNull private final Bar bar1;\n    @NonNull private final Bar bar2;\n    public Foo(@NonNull final Bar bar1, @NonNull final Bar bar2) {\n      enforceConsistency();\n      this.bar1 \u003d bar1;\n      this.bar2 \u003d bar2;\n    }\n\n    private void enforceConsistency() {\n      bar1.enforceConsistency();\n    }\n  }\n\nbar1 is final @NonNull, and still this code will crash with NPE.\n\nOf course your current code doesn\u0027t have such a bug, but all it takes to introduce it is to move the assignment of mRequests in l.5405 together with all the other assignments. And it won\u0027t crash, it will only behave incorrectly – which won\u0027t be caught by tests, because at this point we don\u0027t have any for this code.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5484,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 5484,
        "endChar": 43
      },
